<Layouts.marketing current_page={:privacy}>
  <section class="m-hero" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
    <div class="m-container">
      <div class="m-eyebrow">Privacy Policy</div>
      <h1>How we handle your personal data.</h1>
      <p class="m-lede">
        This policy explains how Merstar International (Singapore) Pte Ltd collects, uses,
        discloses and protects personal data in line with Singapore's Personal Data Protection
        Act 2012 (PDPA).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="m-section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="m-container">
      <div class="m-legal">
        <p class="m-legal-updated">Last updated: 9 October 2026</p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Merstar International (Singapore) Pte Ltd (UEN 198901368N) ("Merstar", "we", "us") is a
          freight forwarding and logistics company at 7 Airline Road #02-09, Cargo Agents
          Building E, Changi Airfreight Centre, Singapore 819834. This policy covers personal data
          we collect through this website and in the course of handling your enquiries and
          shipments.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Personal data we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect personal data that you give us, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name, company, job title, email address and phone number;</li>
          <li>
            details you include in a contact or quote request, such as shipment origin and
            destination, cargo details and any message you send us;
          </li>
          <li>
            information needed to arrange a shipment, such as shipper and consignee names,
            addresses and contact details, and customs documentation.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you visit the website, our hosting provider records basic technical data such as
          your IP address, browser type and the pages requested, for security and to keep the site
          running.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>We use your personal data to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>respond to your enquiries and prepare quotations;</li>
          <li>arrange, track and deliver shipments, including customs clearance;</li>
          <li>manage our relationship with you and your organisation, including billing;</li>
          <li>meet our legal, regulatory and customs obligations; and</li>
          <li>keep this website secure and working properly.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We will not use your personal data for any other purpose without first telling you and,
          where required, getting your consent.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Consent</h2>
        <p>
          By submitting a form on this website or otherwise giving us your personal data, you
          consent to us collecting, using and disclosing it for the purposes above. If you give us
          personal data about someone else, such as a consignee, please make sure they have agreed
          to this.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can withdraw your consent at any time by contacting our Data Protection Officer
          (section 11). We will tell you what withdrawal means for you; for example, we may no
          longer be able to handle a shipment or respond to an enquiry. Withdrawal does not affect
          processing we must carry out by law.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Marketing</h2>
        <p>
          We will only send you marketing messages if you have agreed to receive them, and every
          message will tell you how to opt out. We comply with the Do Not Call provisions of the
          PDPA and will not send marketing messages to Singapore telephone numbers on the Do Not
          Call Registry without your clear consent.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>We share personal data only as needed for the purposes above, with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            airlines, shipping lines, hauliers, warehouses and overseas agents, including members of
            the L.I.N.K Global Network, who help move your shipment;
          </li>
          <li>customs and other government authorities, where required by law;</li>
          <li>
            service providers who run our systems for us, such as website hosting and email
            delivery providers; and
          </li>
          <li>professional advisers, auditors and insurers.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal data.</p>

        <h2>7. Transfers outside Singapore</h2>
        <p>
          Freight forwarding is international, so personal data may be sent to agents, carriers
          and authorities in the countries a shipment passes through. This website and our email
          services are also hosted by providers whose servers may be outside Singapore. Where we
          transfer personal data overseas, we take steps to ensure it receives a standard of
          protection comparable to the PDPA, as the Act requires.
        </p>

        <h2>8. How we protect it</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable security arrangements to protect personal data from unauthorised
          access, collection, use, disclosure, copying, modification or disposal. These include
          encrypted connections (HTTPS) for this website and limiting access to staff and service
          providers who need it. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure,
          so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>9. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep personal data only for as long as it serves the purposes it was collected for or
          is needed for legal, accounting or customs reasons. When it is no longer needed, we
          delete or anonymise it.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Access and correction</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask to see the personal data we hold about you, how it has been used or disclosed
          in the past year, or to correct any errors. Please write to our Data Protection Officer.
          We will respond as soon as reasonably possible, normally within 30 days, and may charge
          a reasonable fee for access requests, which we will tell you about first. Please help
          us keep your data accurate by letting us know if it changes.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact our Data Protection Officer</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about this policy, to withdraw consent, or to request access or
          correction, contact:
        </p>
        <div class="m-card m-legal-contact">
          <p><strong>Data Protection Officer</strong></p>
          <p>Merstar International (Singapore) Pte Ltd</p>
          <p>
            7 Airline Road #02-09, Cargo Agents Building E,<br />
            Changi Airfreight Centre, Singapore 819834
          </p>
          <p>
            Email: <a href="mailto:dpo@merstar.com.sg" class="m-link">dpo@merstar.com.sg</a>
          </p>
          <p>Phone: <a href="tel:+6565458833" class="m-link">(65) 6545-8833</a></p>
        </div>
        <p>
          If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the Personal Data Protection
          Commission at <a href="https://www.pdpc.gov.sg" class="m-link">www.pdpc.gov.sg</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Cookies and third-party content</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses only the cookies it needs to work, such as a session cookie that
          protects forms against misuse. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies. Fonts are
          loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser connects to Google's servers when you view the
          site.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this
          page, with the date it was last updated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.marketing>
